{"review":"draft","flags":[{"page":26,"note":"'As K approaches the total number of instances, error function drops down to 0' is inaccurate: training error is 0 at k = 1; at k = N every point gets the majority class."},{"page":27,"note":"The kernel is written w = 1/d(xq, xi)² while the formula image elsewhere shows 1/d; the lesson uses 1/d² as in the worked example."},{"page":29,"note":"The problem-2 distance adds a Euclidean term (income, locality) to a nominal-mismatch fraction; this is a custom mixed distance, not Gower. The lesson follows the slide."},{"page":8,"note":"The scatter on p.8 shows 15 points but the table lists 13; the lab uses the 13 tabulated points."}],"recall":{"defs":[["Instance-based learning","Predict from stored examples similar to the query."],["k-NN","Vote or average over the k closest training points."],["Minkowski distance","L_h norm of the difference vector."],["Gower distance","Mixed-type average dissimilarity in [0, 1]."],["Locally weighted regression","Kernel-weighted local fit for each query."],["Cross-validation","Repeated train/validate splits averaged."]],"formulas":["\\hat f(x_q)=\\arg\\max_v\\sum_{i=1}^k\\delta(v,f(x_i))","\\hat f(x_q)=\\frac{\\sum w_if(x_i)}{\\sum w_i},\\ w_i=\\frac1{d(x_q,x_i)^2}","d(i,j)=\\left(\\sum_f|x_{if}-x_{jf}|^h\\right)^{1/h}","d_{asym}=\\frac{r+s}{q+r+s}","E_3(x_q)=\\tfrac12\\sum_{kNN}(f-\\hat f)^2K(d(x_q,x))"],"takeaways":["Lazy learners store data and decide at query time.","Distance choice and feature scaling define what 'nearest' means.","Choose k by validation; weight closer neighbours; beware high dimensions.","LWR fits a fresh kernel-weighted model per query.","Tune on validation folds (k-fold CV) and use the test set once."],"confused":[["Validation vs test set","Tuning vs final estimate."],["Symmetric vs asymmetric binary","0-0 matches count vs ignored."],["k in k-NN vs k in k-fold","Neighbours vs number of folds."],["LWR vs k-NN regression","Local weighted line vs local average."]],"minute":"Instance-based learners keep the training data and predict by similarity. k-NN votes among the k nearest points for classes or averages them for numbers; distance-weighted k-NN lets close points count more. 'Near' depends on the distance: Minkowski (Manhattan, Euclidean, supremum) for numbers after scaling, matching or Jaccard for categorical and binary data, Gower for mixed records. High dimensions break distances, so select or weight features. Choose k by validation (√N is a start), use locally weighted regression for smooth curves, and always select models with validation or k-fold cross-validation, keeping the test set for one final estimate."},"flashcards":[["Lazy vs eager","Less training/more predicting vs more training/less predicting",5],["k-NN prediction","Vote (discrete) or mean/median (real)",8],["Simple matching (nominal)","$d=\\frac{p-m}{p}$",11],["Asymmetric binary distance","$\\frac{r+s}{q+r+s}$",12],["Jaccard similarity","$\\frac{q}{q+r+s}$",12],["Minkowski distance","$\\left(\\sum_f|x_{if}-x_{jf}|^h\\right)^{1/h}$",14],["Metric properties","Positive definiteness, symmetry, triangle inequality",14],["h = 1, 2, ∞","Manhattan, Euclidean, supremum",15],["Ordinal to [0,1]","$\\frac{r-1}{M-1}$",18],["Gower distance","Weighted average of per-attribute dissimilarities in [0,1]",19],["Rule of thumb for k","$\\sqrt N$",24],["Distance-weighted kernel","$w_i=1/d(x_q,x_i)^2$",27],["LWR gradient","$\\Delta w_j=\\eta\\sum K(d)(f-\\hat f)a_j$",37],["Train / validation / test","Fit / select & tune / final assessment",45],["k-fold CV","Rotate k held-out folds and average",49]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["what","h1"],"deep":["i-ibl"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h2"],"deep":["i-knn"],"viz":["knnLab"],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h1"],"deep":["i-matrices"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["i-nominal"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h4"],"deep":["i-binary"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["h3"],"deep":["i